# Plot text layout — NO OVERLAPS

**Hard rule:** never ship a figure with overlapping or colliding text (titles, tick labels, legends, annotations, section banners, axis labels). Overlap is a failure; fix and re-save.

**ALWAYS LOOK AT THE FIGURE** after generation — open or `Read` the saved PNG and confirm visually. If anything overlaps, clips, or runs into data, fix layout and regenerate. Do not finish the turn while overlaps remain.

## Before saving

1. **Inspect the output** — open or read the saved PNG; fix overlap before finishing.
2. **Use shared helpers** — prefer `viz/plot_layout.py` (`apply_category_tick_labels`, `finalize_grid_figure`, `set_ylabel_multiline`, `save_figure`) for comparison grids and box plots.
3. **Prefer reserved space over floating labels** — put section titles in their own gridspec row (blank axes + `text`), not `fig.text` at a guessed y that can land on tick labels.

## Tick labels

- **Rotate or hide** when labels are long or numerous (≥4 conditions, or any label >9 chars).
- **Bottom row only** — in multi-row grids, show x tick labels on the bottom row only; hide on upper rows.
- **Alignment** — use `ha="right"` with rotation ≥20° so rotated labels sit under their tick.
- **Font size** — reduce tick fontsize (7–8) before accepting overlap.
- With **4+ categories**, expect rotated labels and raise `bottom` / nested `hspace` so they never collide with the row below.

## Axis and title spacing

- Prefer **multiline y-labels** over long single-line strings.
- Use plain ASCII in labels when unicode causes clipping (`full hidden` not `ℝᴴ`).
- Set explicit `subplots_adjust` / nested `hspace` / `wspace` and `pad_inches` on save; do not rely on defaults alone.
- Leave room for `suptitle` with `top` ≤ 0.84 (often 0.72–0.80 when panel titles are multi-line) and `fig.suptitle(..., y=0.98)`.
- **Never** save with `bbox_inches="tight"` after setting explicit margins — it collapses the headroom reserved for the suptitle and reintroduces title overlap. Use `viz.plot_layout.save_figure` (no tight crop).
- Put legends **outside** data when they would cover curves (e.g. `lower left` early in training, or `bbox_to_anchor` outside the axes).

## Annotations

- Keep panel annotations ≤3 lines when panels are small; shrink fontsize (5–6) or abbreviate.
- Use `bbox` with background when text crosses data.
- Do not place a mid-figure banner on top of PCA x-axis labels — use a dedicated gridspec band.
- **Never** put motif/DFA/arrow schematics on the same axes as a title. Use separate gridspec bands: title | schematic | data.

## Do not

- Ship figures with overlapping x tick labels (common failure mode in condition comparisons).
- Add new one-off layout logic when `viz/plot_layout.py` can be extended instead.
- Claim a multi-panel figure is done without a visual check of **every** panel including mid-figure section titles.
- End a turn after generating a figure without `Read`-ing the PNG/JPG for overlaps (see `figures-no-overlaps.mdc`).
